            <ArticleTitle>A rare case of late solitary vertebral metastasis from an adenoid cystic carcinoma of the lacrimal gland.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr-2016-218371</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2016-218371</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adenoid cystic carcinoma of the lacrimal gland is one among the common malignancies affecting the lacrimal gland. However, overall, it is a rare condition. It has a rather poor prognosis with local recurrence and distant haematological metastasis which are invariably multiple. We present a rare case of a 51-year-old woman who presented with localised lower thoracic pain with collapse of the T10 vertebral body, which turned out be a solitary late metastasis from her previously treated lacrimal gland tumour.</AbstractText>
